real wage rises and improved living standards.’ Using the data in the extracts and your knowledge of economics, assess the view that the government should make raising productivity a priority in order to improve living standards in the UK.","topics":["2-2-6-determinants-of-long-run-aggregate-supply"],"board":"aqa","groups":["macroeconomics"],"keywords":["productivity","real wages","long-run aggregate supply"],"qpPage":3,"msPage":9,"ctxPage":2,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"aqa-as-p2-2024-jun-q7","p":87,"section":"A","questionNumber":"7","parentQuestion":null,"choiceGroup":null,"marks":1,"questionText":"Which one of the following is most likely to cause a rightward shift of the long-run aggregate supply curve?","topics":["2-2-6-determinants-of-long-run-aggregate-supply"],"board":"aqa","groups":["macroeconomics"],"keywords":["long-run aggregate supply","labour mobility"],"qpPage":4,"msPage":3,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null,"type":"mcq","options":["A fall in the supply of credit","A reduction in geographical immobility of labour","A rise in the cost of new technology","An increase in welfare benefit payments"],"usesFigure":false},{"id":"aqa-p3-2024-jun-q23","p":70,"section":"A","questionNumber":"23","parentQuestion":null,"choiceGroup":null,"marks":1,"questionText":"Figure 7 shows two long-run aggregate supply curves (LRAS) for an economy. Which one of the following is most likely to explain the shift of the long-run aggregate supply curve from LRAS1 to LRAS2?","topics":["2-2-6-determinants-of-long-run-aggregate-supply","2-2-2-aggregate-demand-and-aggregate-supply-analysis"],"board":"aqa","groups":["macroeconomics"],"keywords":["long-run aggregate supply","immigration","labour force"],"qpPage":17,"msPage":3,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null,"type":"mcq","options":["A reduction in the basic and higher rates of income tax","A reduction in the geographical mobility of labour","An increase in immigration","An increase in imports of goods and services"],"usesFigure":true},{"i